# Netlify response headers.
#
# The Batted Ball Trajectory Tool runs R in the browser (Shinylive/webR).
# webR loads the files under vfs/ (fonts, fontconfig, R library files) lazily
# and sizes each one from its Content-Length header. Netlify compresses some of
# these (for example font/ttf) with Brotli and drops Content-Length, so webR
# sees them as empty files and every character in a plot is drawn as a missing
# glyph box. Serving them as plain binary keeps Netlify from compressing them.
# Update the shinylive version in the path if the extension is upgraded.
/site_libs/quarto-contrib/shinylive-0.9.1/shinylive/webr/vfs/*
  Content-Type: application/octet-stream
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, no-transform
